# DVC-only data repo: git tracks DVC pointers + metadata, never raw data.
#
# Denylist-by-default: ignore everything at the repo root, then re-include
# only the files git should hold. This can't go stale when a new result
# folder or a new file type appears (which is what let raw data leak in
# before). Raw data lives in the DVC cache + lakeFS; git carries only the
# *.dvc pointers that reference it.

# Ignore everything at the repo root by default.
/*

# Re-include only what git should track: DVC pointers, docs, and config.
# (Comments must be on their own line; gitignore has no inline comments.)
!/*.dvc
!/*.md
!/.gitignore
!/.dvcignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.dvc/
